IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- SwiftUI-native, adaptive (ADR-002/006): ScrollView + width-capped column;
  footer reflows row<->stack on iOS compact width (OnboardingPage.isCompact).
- Design tokens only (P2): Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius; SwiftUI
  material via TSGlassPanel (web glass, ADR-005). No hardcoded colors/typography.
- i18n (ADR-014): static literals via LocalizedStringKey; dynamic checklist keys
  via OnboardingText.localized (String(localized:)) — web key names preserved 1:1.
- a11y (ADR-015): decorative step indicators .accessibilityHidden (web aria-hidden);
  header/intro/rows grouped; skip hint as .help + .accessibilityHint; light/dark +
  high-contrast via the dynamic token colors; SF Symbols.
- States: loading (skeleton) + success (checklist). The source has no error/empty
  region — a failed status query degrades to the pessimistic checklist (every
  anchor unmet) exactly as the web query does; modelled by load() catch ->
  OnboardingChecklistStatus.pending and asserted by testFailedLoadDegradesToPessimisticReady.
- Units (P1/S5): none — this page carries no SI measurements.
- Navigation: OnboardingRouteRegistration registers .onboarding; deep-link
  /onboarding resolves via AppRouteParser (asserted by testRouteMetadata). The
  Tesla-account step + "Tesla account page" help link route to .settings (web
  /tesla-account; /account aliases to .settings). Doc links open the install's
  /docs via the system browser (web same-origin href).

